{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:83207","published":"2026-10-14T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-10-29T11:31:01.230438518Z","related":["CVE-2026-45859","CVE-2026-46319","CVE-2026-53011","CVE-2026-63899","CVE-2026-63974","CVE-2026-64030","CVE-2026-64032","CVE-2026-64162","CVE-2026-68140","CVE-2026-68377","CVE-2026-72262","CVE-2026-74574","CVE-2026-74641","CVE-2026-80985","CVE-2026-89526","CVE-2026-89689","CVE-2026-89894","CVE-2026-90036","CVE-2026-93207","CVE-2026-93228"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-45859","CVE-2026-46319","CVE-2026-53011","CVE-2026-63899","CVE-2026-63974","CVE-2026-64030","CVE-2026-64032","CVE-2026-64162","CVE-2026-68140","CVE-2026-68377","CVE-2026-72262","CVE-2026-74574","CVE-2026-74641","CVE-2026-80985","CVE-2026-89526","CVE-2026-89689","CVE-2026-89894","CVE-2026-90036","CVE-2026-93207","CVE-2026-93228"],"summary":"Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: netfilter: nfnetlink_queue: do shared-unconfirmed check before segmentation (CVE-2026-45859)\n  * kernel: net/sched: act_ct: Only release RCU read lock after ct_ft (CVE-2026-46319)\n  * kernel: net/sched: taprio: fix use-after-free in advance_sched() on schedule switch (CVE-2026-53011)\n  * kernel: USB: serial: mxuport: fix memory corruption with small endpoint (CVE-2026-63899)\n  * kernel: bridge: mcast: Fix a possible use-after-free when removing a bridge port (CVE-2026-64032)\n  * kernel: wifi: mac80211: bounds-check link_id in ieee80211_ml_epcs (CVE-2026-64030)\n  * kernel: Bluetooth: hci_sync: Set HCI_CMD_DRAIN_WORKQUEUE during device close (CVE-2026-63974)\n  * kernel: idpf: fix read_dev_clk_lock spinlock init in idpf_ptp_init() (CVE-2026-64162)\n  * kernel: Linux kernel: Denial of Service due to use-after-free in act_tunnel_key (CVE-2026-68377)\n  * kernel: net/iucv: fix use-after-free of a severed iucv_path (CVE-2026-68140)\n  * kernel: ASoC: SOF: ipc3-control: Fix heap overflow in bytes_ext put/get (CVE-2026-72262)\n  * kernel: dmaengine: idxd: fix fdev setup failure cleanup in idxd_cdev_open() (CVE-2026-74574)\n  * kernel: ALSA: usx2y: bound the hwdep mmap fault offset (CVE-2026-74641)\n  * kernel: net/smc: carry oversized SMC-Rv2 LLC messages in the queue entry (CVE-2026-80985)\n  * kernel: svcrdma: Validate Read chunk positions before reconstruction (CVE-2026-89526)\n  * kernel: nfsd: don't free session slots that are still in use (CVE-2026-89689)\n  * kernel: NFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during blocked-lock reaping (CVE-2026-90036)\n  * kernel: media: cx231xx: reject geometry changes while the VBI queue is busy (CVE-2026-89894)\n  * kernel: SUNRPC: Zero rpc_gss_wire_cred at svcauth_gss_decode_credbody() entry (CVE-2026-93207)\n  * kernel: svcrdma: Reject Write/Reply chunks with segcount 0 (CVE-2026-93228)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * cannot use VFs of i40e/ice NIC in bond device (JIRA:AlmaLinux-143410)\n  * ionic: commit backported to 9.8 missing in 10.2 (JIRA:AlmaLinux-165657)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.12.0-211.66.1.el10_2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:83207.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-64k","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-64k"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.12.0-211.66.1.el10_2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:83207.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-64k-core","ecosystem":"Alm